

# Drift reports are derived data — regenerated on every /doc-sync run.
# The snapshot itself (doc-snapshot/pages/, manifest.json, CHANGELOG.md)
# IS committed; it is the baseline every diff is taken against.
doc-snapshot/reports/

# ── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The LangGraph dev server reads backend/.env (declared by backend/langgraph.json).
# Nothing here is ever committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Recording output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Clips are build output: reproducible from autorecorder/ plus `npm run record`,
# ~5MB each and rewritten on every re-record. Committing them took one sibling
# repo's .git to 348MB before its history had to be rewritten.
#
# The rule is `*.webm`, NOT the directory: videos/manifest.json and
# videos/MANIFEST.md live there too and are meant to be committed — they are the
# record of which clips are current. Ignoring the folder hid them.
autorecorder/videos/*.webm
autorecorder/videos/logs/
autorecorder/videos/RECORD_RESULTS*.json
autorecorder/videos/RUN_REPORT.*

# Generated after install by ci/write-versions.mjs — it describes one run.
frontend/VERSIONS.md

# The daily QA report describes one run, like the clips it cites. Regenerate it
# with `npm run report`; commit it only if you want a dated record in git.
DOCUMENTED_REPORT.md

# ── TEMPORARY: CI/CD excluded for the merge into another repo ───────────────
# This block is temporary. It exists so this tree can be merged into a repo
# that must not carry the pipeline. Delete the whole block to restore.
#
# Scope is deliberately not "all of ci/". That folder is not purely CI: the
# harness itself shells into it, so removing it wholesale breaks local
# commands. Only the scripts that nothing but GitHub Actions calls are listed.
#
#   kept, and why:
#     ci/check-doc-drift.mjs   npm run drift / drift:sync
#     ci/write-versions.mjs    npm run record:doctor (autorecorder calls it)
#     ci/build-report.mjs      npm run report
#     ci/lib/                  imported by the three above
#     ci/mux.mjs               npm run mux -- the manual re-mux entry point;
#                              CI muxes via automate.mjs and never calls it
#
# NOTE: .gitignore does not untrack files git already knows about. These are
# all committed, so this block alone changes nothing. To actually drop them:
#   git rm -r --cached .github/workflows ci/automate.mjs ci/run-name.mjs \
#     ci/resolve-selection.mjs ci/list-pages.mjs ci/validate-pages.mjs
.github/workflows/
ci/automate.mjs
ci/run-name.mjs
ci/resolve-selection.mjs
ci/list-pages.mjs
ci/validate-pages.mjs
